        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e67babf4-39cc-3ae1-8ff6-734483344b1c> ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      "a broken twill, but relatively few warps."@en , "Woven silk brocade, with vertical and horizontal point repeat with 4 minimum pattern areas.  Satin foundation structure: 4/1 satin, warp count: 70, ivory silk.  weft: cotton, 2 ply Z twist.  Satin and velvet warp order 3-1-3.  Velvet structure"@en , "red and green silk, pile counts, warps 8, along weft 8.  Binding weft threads: silk, ivory.  Brocade structure: part brocaded, 4/1 twill, count 9.  Shots between pile 2, brocaded only in the spandrels and in the centre of the medallion.  Selvedges: cotton weft shows"@en ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/900> , <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/617> ;
